Why each is unguarded (root cause, so the fix is unambiguous):

3a. trends.go:44 -- the sumByExpense PIN-MATCH branch. Every committed test
    that reaches MajorExpenseTrends with a refund passes pins = nil:
      $ grep -rn "MajorExpenseTrends(" --include=*_test.go
        trends_test.go:542 MajorExpenseTrends(ts, defs, nil, ...)
        trends_test.go:592 MajorExpenseTrends(ts, defs, pins, ...)   <- only pin test
        trends_test.go:614 MajorExpenseTrends(ts, nil, nil, ...)
        trends_test.go:636 MajorExpenseTrends(ts, defs, nil, ...)
        trends_test.go:666 MajorExpenseTrends(ts, defs, nil, ...)
        .swarm/tier3/CB3/cb3_oracle_test.go:139  (pins = nil)
    The one pin test, TestAnalyzeMajorExpenseTrends_PinOverridesKeyword
    (trends_test.go:573-608), uses a single Amount: -150 row, so signed net
    and abs both give 150 -- it cannot distinguish the two forms. The
    manifest's claim that regressions cover "sumByExpense's two sites" is
    therefore only true for the keyword-match branch.
    This is a LIVE production path, not dead code: mcpsvc/spend/trends.go:184
    calls insights.MajorExpenseTrends(ts, defs, pins, start, end) with real
    pins for the get_trends major_expense_trends surface.

3b. trends.go:320 -- SpendingVelocity spentSoFar. models.SpendingVelocity
    (internal/models/insights.go:41-47) has no SpentSoFar field, so the only
    observable is MonthProjection = spentSoFar + dailyAvg*daysRemaining, and
    TestCalculateSpendingVelocity_RefundDominantPeriodIsNegative asserts only
    `MonthProjection >= 0 -> error`. Measured with a throwaway probe on the
    test's own fixture (today 2026-09-02, DaysRemaining=28):
        unmutated  MonthProjection = -15950.00
        mutated    MonthProjection = -14850.00
    Both negative -> the assertion passes either way. The dailyAvg term
    (-550*28) swamps the +/-550 spentSoFar term. Note this guard is also
    date-fragile: at month end (daysRemaining ~ 0) the mutated value would be
    +550 and the test would fail, so the coverage such as it is depends on the
    calendar. A direct assertion is needed -- e.g. pin MonthProjection to its
    exact expected value, or exercise a fixture where the spentSoFar sign
    determines the outcome.

CRITERION 3 VERDICT: FAIL. The spec requires "Committed regression tests per
site" and the task requires at least one committed test to fail per reverted
site; 2 of 8 sites have none. Behavior is correct today; the guard is absent.

